    moduleId: "tunnels", order: 1, slug: "ssh-management-hardening", title: "SSH Management-Plane Hardening", summary: "Reduce SSH attack surface with keys, scoped listeners and sources, least privilege, validated policy, logging, and safe rollback.", capabilities: ["LIN-9.1"], minutes: 30,
    outcomes: ["Build a key-based SSH baseline with narrow user and source policy.", "Validate effective configuration, file permissions, listener exposure, and authentication logs before disabling weaker methods."],
    model: "SSH hardening layers network exposure, server configuration, host identity, user authentication, authorization, privilege, logging, and recovery. No single directive replaces source filtering, patched software, key protection, or monitored access.",
