    model: "VXLAN encapsulates Ethernet frames in UDP over an IP underlay and identifies the overlay segment with a 24-bit VNI. Linux can use static flood-list entries or control-plane-learned mappings. MACsec protects Ethernet frames on a directly connected link; it does not provide end-to-end routed encryption or replace VXLAN control-plane design.",
